# run logs
*.log

# rendered intermediates
report/_*.png

# build outputs that are regenerated (the submitted PDF is kept deliberately)
report/~$*

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# never commit dataset content: the AI Village corpus is gated and its terms
# forbid redistribution. Only derived aggregate statistics (facts_*.json) are kept.
*.jsonl
*.jsonl.gz
*.parquet
data/

# Exported event trains are a close derivative of a gated corpus: exact per-agent timestamps for
# every message in the window. The AI Village research terms forbid redistributing the corpus, and
# while this carries no text and no identities, the timing structure is substantial enough that
# shipping it would be redistribution in substance. The exporter is committed instead, so anyone
# with their own dataset access can regenerate it in one command.
cotete_export/*_events.json
cotete_export/*_trains.csv
cotete_export/export_summary.json

# The continuous-time results carry the corpus's own agent and room UUIDs, 32 of them. Every
# committed facts_*.json in this repository contains zero such identifiers, because the policy here
# is that only derived aggregate statistics are released. Keeping these out preserves that. The
# aggregate result the paper actually cites is committed as facts_cotete.json, with agents under
# opaque labels, and the scripts are documented so anyone with their own dataset access can
# regenerate the full per-pair file.
cotete_export/cotete_results.json
cotete_export/cotete_te_matrix_*.csv

# LaTeX build artifacts. main.tex, the figures and main.pdf are kept; the rest is regenerated by
# pdflatex and was committed by accident once already.
arxiv/*.aux
arxiv/*.log
arxiv/*.out
arxiv/*.bbl
arxiv/*.blg
arxiv/*.toc
arxiv/*.fls
arxiv/*.fdb_latexmk
arxiv/*.synctex.gz
